ry Stream showing partner cards and free seat counts.\r\n   - Active Shared Trips Console with Route Alignment Match Badging (e.g. \"94% Route Match\").\r\n   - Fast Identity Search Bar (supporting Driver IDs like #101 and Booking Refs like NX-501) + \"Revert Last Confirmation\" Undo control.\r\n\r\n4. Tab 4: \"City Sustainability Analytics\" (Focus: Enterprise & Environmental Metrics)\r\n   - Comprehensive climate metrics: Net CO2 reduced (kg), single-d\n<truncated 807 bytes>\n6. Please upgrade the \"NexusMobility — Smart City Eco-Logistics\" web platform with the following visual, interactive, and user experience enhancements across index.html, styles.css, and app.js:\r\n\r\n1. Clean Header & Navigation Cleanup:\r\n   - Remove the \"Export Package (.ZIP)\" button from the top navigation header bar. Keep only the essential primary controls (\"Rush-Hour Simulation\" and \"Book Eco-Ride\").\r\n\r\n2. Replace 3D Mouse Tilt with Smooth 2D Hover Lifting:\r\n   - Remove the heavy 3D perspective mouse-tracking tilt effect to eliminate card stuttering and dizziness.\r\n   - Replace it with a smooth 2D micro-lifting hover transition (`transform: translateY(-4px);` with a soft emerald/slate glow shadow).\r\n\r\n3. Enhanced Spatial Map & Route Direction Indicators:\r\n   - Update the metropolitan route map canvas to display clear directional path indicators (e.g. animated directional flow arrows along active corridors) showing transit direction from Origin to Destination.\r\n   - Increase station node visibility with distinct station hub icons and clear zone tags.\r\n\r\n4. Animated Car Running Across Spatial Map Routes:\r\n   - Add a smooth, animated top-down car icon (with a subtle electric glow/headlight trail) that drives along calculated route nodes on the 3D map canvas upon confirming a ride or auto-dispatching a trip.\r\n\r\n5. Background Particle Animation:\r\n   - Add a subtle, ambient background Canvas layer rendering slow-floating green leaf particles and light electric energy nodes floating upward across the soft slate backdrop.\r\n\r\n6. Friendly Eco-Mascot Character (\"EcoSprout\"):\r\n   - Introduce a fun, friendly eco-mascot character (\"EcoSprout\" wearing a leaf hat and driving gogg\n<truncated 599 bytes>\n7. # TASK: Create C++ Backend Server for NexusMobility Eco-Logistics Platform\r\n\r\n## Objective\r\nConvert the front-end state engine (`app.js`) of the NexusMobility application into a modern, thread-safe C++ REST API server. The C++ backend will handle pathfinding algorithms, data structures (circular buffers, queues, priority matching), trip dispatching, and auditing, while serving JSON responses to the frontend.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🛠️ Architecture & Technical Stack\r\n- **Language Standard**: Modern C++20 / C++17\r\n- **HTTP/REST Framework**: Crow C++ (or CrowCpp / Pistache / httplib)\r\n- **JSON Serialization**: `nlohmann/json`\r\n- **Build System**: CMake (Minimum version 3.16)\r\n- **Data Structures**:\r\n  - `std::vector` and adjacency lists for graph routing\r\n  - Priority Queue / Min-Heap for Dijkstra's shortest path\r\n  - Ring Buffer / Circular Queue (`std::array` or `std::vector` with head/tail pointers) for the 5-Slot Priority Standby Lounge\r\n  - Thread-safe FIFO `std::queue` for the Commuter Dispatch Pipeline\r\n  - `std::stack` or custom vector deque for the Reversal Audit Log\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 📋 Core Modules to Implement in C++\r\n\r\n### 1. Data Models (`Models.hpp`)\r\nDefine clean C++ structs with standard serialization to JSON:\r\n- `Station`: `id` (string), `name` (string), `x` (double), `y` (double), `z` (double), `zone` (string), `icon` (string)\r\n- `Corridor`: `u` (string), `v` (string), `distance` (double)\r\n- `Passenger`: `id` (string), `name` (string), `pickup` (string), `drop` (string), `requestedAt` (string), `status` (string)\r\n- `Driver`: `id` (int), `name` (string), `station` (string), `seats` (int), `originalSeats` (int), `tripsCompleted` (int)\r\n- `Trip`: `tripRef` (stri\n<truncated 2821 bytes>\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Request:** Convert the frontend state engine (`app.js`) of \"NexusMobility — Smart City Eco-Logistics\" into a modern, production-grade, thread-safe C++ REST API server.\n- **Key Responsibilities:**\n  - Implement Dijkstra's shortest path with Min-Heap for eco-route calculation.\n  - Implement custom data structures: 5-slot priority standby ring buffer (`std::array`), commuter FIFO dispatch pipeline (`std::queue`/`std::deque`), fleet management, and LIFO rollback stack (`revertLatestConfirmation`).\n  - Serve all operations as JSON REST endpoints via modern C++ HTTP framework (`cpp-httplib`) with CORS support.\n  - Connect and document endpoints mirroring the front-end features without displaying academic/backend CS jargon to the front-facing UI.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Created C++ Backend Architecture (`C:\\Users\\Kartik Bhosle\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a\\cpp-backend\\`):**\n  - `include/Models.hpp`: Complete C++ struct models with bidirectional `nlohmann::json` serialization (`Station`, `Corridor`, `Passenger`, `Driver`, `Trip`, `AuditAction`, `RouteResult`, `EcoLeader`).\n  - `include/NexusEngine.hpp`: Singleton thread-safe core engine interface with mutex synchronization.\n  - `src/NexusEngine.cpp`: Implementation of:\n    - Dijkstra pathfinding algorithm with Min-Heap (`std::priority_queue`).\n    - Dynamic commuter fare splitting, time estimation, and CO₂ offset formula.\n    - Commuter FIFO queue (`submitRideRequest`, `dequeueNextRequest`).\n    - Fixed 5-slot circular ring buffer with modulo indexing (`(idx + 1) % 5`) and overflow protection.\n    - Driver onboarding, fleet registry, O(1) identity verification (`verifyRecord`).\n    - Route compatibility scoring and LIFO rollback stack (`revertLatestConfirmation`).\n    - One-click `loadRushHourDemo` scenario loader.\n  - `src/main.cpp`: Complete REST API server implementation using `cpp-httplib` handling 22 distinct JSON API endpoints with full CORS preflight support.\n  - `CMakeLists.txt`: Modern CMake 3.16+ configuration using `FetchContent` for `nlohmann/json` and `cpp-httplib`, Winsock2 libraries for Windows (`ws2_32`, `wsock32`), and POSIX threads.\n  - `README.md`: Comprehensive API manual with curl examples and payload schemas.\n  - `build.bat` & `run.bat`: Windows batch scripts for automated building and launching.\n  - `test_api.ps1` & `test_api.sh`: Complete PowerShell and Bash automated API integration test suites.\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Environment & Tool Constraints:** The environment shell command tool encountered `powershell: executable file not found in %PATH%` on the host runner. Direct compilation execution via `run_command` failed because the powershell binary is not directly exposed in the tool PATH. Thus, full self-contained build scripts (`CMakeLists.txt`, `build.bat`, `run.bat`, `test_api.ps1`, `test_api.sh`) were provided alongside standard headers.\n- **Dependencies:** Used `cpp-httplib` and `nlohmann/json` as they support clean header-only inclusion and automatic `FetchContent` in CMake without requiring manual package manager installations.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- All C++ source code, models, engine logic, server setup, and build files are fully written to disk under `cpp-backend/`.\n- Frontend files (`index.html`, `styles.css`, `app.js`) currently run locally and can be configured to point to `http://localhost:8080/api` if connected to this C++ backend.\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Frontend Integration (Optional/Follow-up):** Update `app.js` with an optional toggle/fetch hook (`USE_CPP_BACKEND = true`) allowing `app.js` to asynchronously query `http://localhost:8080/api` when the C++ server is running, while falling back gracefully to client-side logic if offline.\n2. **Verification & Delivery:** Present the completed C++ backend implementation, API endpoint reference, build instructions, and verification script to the user.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- The C++ backend strictly conforms to the requested architecture: C++17/20, `nlohmann/json`, CMake, Dijkstra with Min-Heap, 5-slot ring buffer, FIFO queue, and LIFO audit stack.\n- The user interface must maintain 100% natural transit and logistics semantics (no backend CS jargon on user-facing endpoints/screens).\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 17 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: README]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/README.md\nLast Edited: 2026-10-17T19:58:45Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: app]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/app.js\nLast Edited: 2026-10-17T19:58:32Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: CMakeLists]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/CMakeLists.txt\nLast Edited: 2026-10-20T06:09:25Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: README]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/README.md\nLast Edited: 2026-10-20T06:10:22Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: build]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/build.bat\nLast Edited: 2026-10-20T06:10:35Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: Models]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/include/Models.hpp\nLast Edited: 2026-10-20T06:07:46Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: NexusEngine]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/include/NexusEngine.hpp\nLast Edited: 2026-10-20T06:08:00Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: run]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/run.bat\nLast Edited: 2026-10-20T06:10:46Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: NexusEngine]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-